# The scenes of the fuzzing deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# fuzzing.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in fuzzing.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add *Jazzer's* JUnit support to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/jazzer/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the dependency
note "Step 2: add it to the lesson, for the tests."
show lessons/fuzzing/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 10

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: *today's* label reader."
show TodaysLabelReader 12 24 "today's label reader" --zoom 20-22

## Scene 4: the example tests
note "The *example* tests: lines someone typed."
show LabelExamplesTest 12 31 "the example tests" --zoom 17-18

## Scene 5: the fuzz test
note "The *fuzz* test: read the line, or refuse it. Nothing else."
show LabelReaderFuzzTest 12 24 "the fuzz test" --zoom 16-23

## Scene 6: the fuzzer finds a crash
note "Fuzz today's reader:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:fuzzing:fuzz -Pcode=today"
callout "Jazzer found a line nobody wrote: an empty postcode crashes the reader."

## Scene 7: the crash, kept as a test
note "Keep the line Jazzer found, and replay it in every test run:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:fuzzing:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The example tests pass. The kept line fails, naming the exception."

## Scene 8: the fixed reader
note "The *fixed* reader refuses what it can't read:"
show FixedLabelReader 17 29 "the fixed reader" --zoom 24-27
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:fuzzing:test"
callout "The kept line is refused now, with the reason, and every test passes."
